A.1.17. {"problem": "The description says a deputy is one \"the owner has named while they are away\", but nothing in the domain lets the owner name a deputy or records when the owner is away. There is no action, no object or property, and no precondition on approve_commit. Any actor with the deputy role can approve at any time, including while the owner is present, so the request's central rule is not enforced.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.approve_commit (description, actor, preconditions)", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.1.18. {"problem": "The new deputy role has no actor in world.actors, and no scenario shows a deputy approving a commit or being denied. The change check therefore never exercises the new path. Existing scenarios use only the owner.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, world.actors and scenarios (approve-only-after-a-passing-check)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.1.19. {"problem": "The diff sets approve_commit and its two preconditions to status: proposed, but the file after the change shows them as confirmed with the new interview ref L46. The two disagree. If the file is right, the permission change was marked confirmed without the second-person confirmation that confirm_element requires for elements about actions.approve_commit. If the diff is right, the declaration is half-confirmed and the unchanged preconditions lose their confirmed status for no reason.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, actions.approve_commit status, source and preconditions checks-pass and not-approved", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.1.20. {"problem": "The change widens who may approve commits, which alters Authoring's behaviour for its consumers. The domain version stays at 19 and the composition member stays at interface 1. The handoff to Delivery passes approver: actor.id, and Delivery's deploy and verify are limited to the 'approver' role, so a deputy-approved commit's approver identity is not a known Delivery approver.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml version; toprope-self.composition.yaml members/wiring; handoffs.deliver_approved_commit", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
