A.5.17. {"problem": "The change request says the owner names a deputy who approves while the owner is away. Nothing declares that. There is no action for the owner to name or revoke a deputy, no property recording who the deputy is, and no precondition tying approval to the owner being away. The `deputy` role is open to any actor in it at any time, so the description sentence 'a deputy the owner has named while they are away' is prose the model does not enforce.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: roles `deputy`, action `approve_commit` (actor list and description)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.5.18. {"problem": "The diff sets `approve_commit` to `status: proposed` and also sets its `checks-pass` and `not-approved` preconditions to proposed. The post-change file shows all three as `confirmed`, with the new source ref L46. The change to who may approve therefore looks confirmed without the required review. `confirm_element` requires a second person, other than the confirmer, to confirm any element at `actions.approve_commit`. The file and the diff disagree, and the preconditions' L6 quote was never about deputies.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: action `approve_commit` status, source and preconditions; action `confirm_element` rule `permission-needs-second-person`", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.5.19. {"problem": "No actor holds the new `deputy` role, because `world.actors` lists only owner and expert. No scenario shows a deputy approving, or being denied by `checks-pass` or `not-approved`. The new permission is never exercised, and the approve scenario still covers only the owner.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: world.actors, scenarios `approve-only-after-a-passing-check`", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.5.20. {"problem": "A deputy can approve, but every other step of the flow stays owner-only: `check_commit`, `cite_evidence` and `deliver`. A deputy therefore cannot run the change check that approval depends on, which leaves wording-only commits as the only ones they can approve without the owner. The deputy also cannot deliver the commit they approved. The approval is recorded under the deputy's id as approver, and the handoff then passes `actor.id` as the approver to Delivery, whose approver role has only ana. The deputy's approval is therefore not consistently carried through the flow.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml: actions `check_commit`, `cite_evidence`, `deliver`, handoff `deliver_approved_commit`; delivery.domain.yaml roles/world.actors", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
